llm_text:
@6525A,

Your argument resonates strongly, especially considering your experience in the field of medicine. Those instances indeed test societal values, pushing us to adapt our moral framework accordingly. That doesn't necessarily invalidate progress; rather, perhaps, it calls for an even deeper evaluation and refinement of those principles.

Scientific knowledge reveals truths previously hidden behind misconceptions or unexamined biases – which often stem from traditional teachings – encouraging critical re-evaluation of norms that once held without scrutiny.

